1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,760
[A station bell rings out.]

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:09,120
No one spoke. But if the bell goes missing, so does part
of the story.

3
00:00:09,160 --> 00:00:17,040
Foleyfold gives those sounds a place on the timeline.
Select a cue to hear where it belongs.

4
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:23,360
Open a local cut. It starts with a clean cue sheet. The
file stays on this device.

5
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:30,760
Give the bell an in point and an out point. Then write
what you hear, not what you see.

6
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:38,320
The assistant checks this browser. Here, Firebase is not
connected. No model generated this caption.

7
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:45,880
On a configured studio, only the note and its duration
enter the prompt. The default route is device only.

8
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:53,800
The editor can permit cloud fallback for this one
request. A returned suggestion names its source and
still needs review.

9
00:00:53,840 --> 00:01:00,920
Here the editor writes the line by hand. Approve it only
when it describes the moment.

10
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:05,360
[The bell rings. The approved caption clears at the end
of its cue.]

11
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:14,160
The export is a timed WebVTT track. Only approved
captions leave the cutting room.

12
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:17,840
Keep the cut private. Give its sound a voice.
